        {
          "type": "practice",
          "title": "Practice: Write Your Own Final Speech",
          "content": "Imagine Macbeth gets one more chance to speak before his death. Macduff is standing over him. The boughs of Birnam Wood lie around them. Write a 12-line speech in iambic pentameter from Macbeth's mouth that includes: (1) recognition that the witches deceived him; (2) acknowledgment of what he has done to Macduff's family; (3) something — anything — about Lady Macbeth. This is the hardest practice in this course. The strongest attempts will use Shakespeare's diction without copying his lines. Read it aloud. Cut a line. Read it again.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Practice: Write a Speech</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">For Macbeth. In his voice.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"940\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Scene</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Macduff above him. Birnam boughs around. One more chance to speak.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 lines. Iambic pentameter.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"370\" width=\"300\" height=\"280\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Must Include 1</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"465\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The deception</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Witches' lies</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"545\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Equivocation</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"585\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">recognized</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"625\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\"That palter...\"</text><rect x=\"400\" y=\"370\" width=\"300\" height=\"280\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Must Include 2</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"465\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Macduff's family</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"505\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Some kind</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">of reckoning</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Not exoneration</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">— recognition</text><rect x=\"720\" y=\"370\" width=\"300\" height=\"280\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"870\" y=\"415\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Must Include 3</text><text x=\"870\" y=\"465\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lady Macbeth</text><text x=\"870\" y=\"505\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Anything</text><text x=\"870\" y=\"545\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about her</text><text x=\"870\" y=\"585\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Even silence</text><text x=\"870\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about her</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"250\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"725\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Method</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"775\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read aloud after each line — does it scan?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"810\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Use Shakespeare's diction; don't copy his lines</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cut one line. Read it again. Cut another. Read.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">When you cannot cut more, you are done.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">The hardest exercise teaches you the most about what the play does.</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Write inside the play"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "title": "Closing Quote",
          "content": "The play's final words belong to Malcolm: 'So thanks to all at once and to each one, / Whom we invite to see us crown'd at Scone.' Order is restored. The new king will distribute earldoms. The witches are off the stage. But the audience remembers the dagger, the sleepwalking, the head on the pole, and the line that names every authoritarian's interior weather: 'It is a tale told by an idiot, full of sound and fury, signifying nothing.' Macbeth ends. The questions it asks do not.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Closing Quote</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A play that does not close</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"235\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Final Lines — Malcolm at Scone</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">So thanks to all at once and to each one,</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">Whom we invite to see us crown'd at Scone.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Order. Civility. Fluorish. Exeunt.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"450\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"495\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What This Course Has Done</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"545\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read Macbeth in Jacobean context</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tracked the seduction through Act I</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Watched the murder and the broken sleep</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Followed the ghost into Act III's paranoia</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"685\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Returned to the witches; lost Lady Macduff's family</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heard \"tomorrow\" and felt Birnam march</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"755\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mapped the themes, productions, and curse</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"790\" width=\"940\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"835\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You have completed a college Shakespeare seminar on Macbeth</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"875\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The play is now yours to read, perform, argue, teach</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"990\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">\"Fair is foul, and foul is fair.\" Begin again.</text></svg>",
            "caption": "End and beginning"
          }
        }
