        "explanation": "Kurosawa jettisons Shakespeare's language completely but preserves — and often intensifies — the play's meaning through images. The famous ending, in which Washizu (Mifune) is cut down by a storm of arrows from his own turning soldiers, dramatizes the theme of the tyrant abandoned by everyone he ruled more viscerally than any speech could. It shows that fidelity in adaptation is about capturing a work's spirit and themes, not reproducing its exact words.",
