          "type": "diagram",
          "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Direct Your Own Scene</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Every choice must be earned by the text</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"160\" width=\"940\" height=\"95\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\">1  PICK A SCENE</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"233\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Witches (I.iii), dagger (II.i), or sleepwalk (V.i)</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"270\" width=\"940\" height=\"290\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\">2  MAKE THE BIG DECISIONS</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"348\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">WITCHES: real, or hallucination? three, or one?</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">DAGGER: show a real blade, or leave the stage empty?</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"424\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">AGE: young &amp; reckless, or old &amp; weary?</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"462\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">BLOOD: show everything, or almost nothing?</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"500\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">ENDING: clean restoration, or the cycle repeats?</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"540\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#888\">These are the exact choices Polanski, Kurosawa, Coen made</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"575\" width=\"940\" height=\"95\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"613\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\">3  WRITE A DIRECTOR'S NOTE</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"648\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">One-sentence idea + justify each choice from the lines</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"685\" width=\"940\" height=\"95\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"723\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\">4  COMPARE TWO STAGINGS</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"758\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Same 20 lines, two ways — watch the meaning shift</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"800\" width=\"800\" height=\"170\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">THE TAKEAWAY</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"897\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No single correct Macbeth —</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"937\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">but readings can illuminate or betray. Go direct it.</text></svg>",
